<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <LangVersion>preview</LangVersion>

    <!-- Pure MAF + Azure OpenAI demo (no AgentEval dependency).
         Versions resolve from Directory.Packages.props (Central Package Management):
         NO Version= attributes here (NU1008), and a package absent from that file
         fails restore with NU1010. Every reference below was checked against it. -->
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Agents.AI" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Agents.AI.Workflows" />
    <!-- MANDATORY, not transitive (MAF 1.17.0). Executor.ConfigureProtocol(ProtocolBuilder) is
         abstract and this source generator emits it; without the reference every custom
         Executor in Workflows/ fails with CS0534. Verified by removing it. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Agents.AI.Workflows.Generators" />
    <PackageReference Include="Azure.AI.OpenAI" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.AI" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.AI.OpenAI" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Memory.Data" />
    <!-- Brute-force cosine over the product index. Already pinned centrally (10.0.9). -->
    <PackageReference Include="System.Numerics.Tensors" />
    <!-- Security: transitive pin (GHSA-g94r-2vxg-569j) -->
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTelemetry.Api" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- The committed PRODUCT vector index (design §D.4 / §G). Generated 2026-09-05 by running
       this project with the "rebuild-embeddings" switch and the embedding-model override
       pointed at text-embedding-3-small (the exact command line is in MEASUREMENT_STATUS §16;
       XML comments cannot carry a double hyphen, so it is not repeated here).
       Real text-embedding-3-small vectors: 99 product documents, 1536 dims, template stamp v2.

       This line and the file land in the SAME commit on purpose — an EmbeddedResource
       pointing at a missing file is a hard build error (MSB3030), which is why it was
       absent until the asset existed.

       ONE asset, since B-21 (2026-09-05). There used to be a second, queries.embeddings.json,
       holding 71 pre-guessed query texts, and PrecomputedEmbeddingSource served queries out
       of it. A query composed at run time is not one of 71 guesses, so it missed, the dense
       leg ranked nothing, and the "real-vectors" path produced 0 in and 0 out for every
       persona. It is deleted. The INDEX is precomputed and committed; the QUERY is embedded
       live at search time against the deployment this file's own model stamp names, and
       EmbeddingSpace proves the two are one space with an identity probe before retrieving.

       The DEFAULT is still ConceptEmbeddingSource (authored concept vectors, deterministic,
       no key, no network) — but for a different reason than before B-21: not because real
       vectors retrieve badly (they do not), but because an Auto that preferred them would
       resolve differently depending on whether a key is present, and a scored suite may not
       change space with the environment. Measured, both spaces, in MEASUREMENT_STATUS §19. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Data\catalogue.embeddings.json" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
